WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:05.510
Nodes are extra modules: oscillators, envelopes, logic, and more.

2
00:00:05.510 --> 00:00:08.544
Right-click empty board space to add one.

3
00:00:08.544 --> 00:00:09.062
An LFO.

4
00:00:09.514 --> 00:00:10.808
Add a Scope beside it.

5
00:00:10.808 --> 00:00:13.631
A scope draws whatever signal passes through it.

6
00:00:14.081 --> 00:00:16.883
Drag the LFO's output into the Scope's input.

7
00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:17.942
There's the wave.

8
00:00:18.392 --> 00:00:20.326
The Scope passes its signal on.

9
00:00:20.326 --> 00:00:24.194
Patch its output into Z Push, and the raster follows the wave.

10
00:00:24.648 --> 00:00:27.784
Turn the LFO's rate knob, and watch the trace speed up.

11
00:00:30.086 --> 00:00:32.858
To remove a node, click its X and confirm.

12
00:00:32.858 --> 00:00:34.310
Its cables go with it.

13
00:00:34.769 --> 00:00:39.076
Every node type is listed in the Node Catalog on the About page.

14
00:00:39.076 --> 00:00:40.422
Next: routing video.
